{"skill":{"slug":"fluid-memory","displayName":"Fluid Memory"},"version":{"version":"1.0.9","createdAt":1772725645999,"changelog":"feat: 更新描述+添加隐私声明","changelogSource":"user","license":null,"files":[{"path":"config.yaml","size":280,"sha256":"3d9143f13d46acd228de344f39f34544d5c01fa6c36c8df7587b892cf7fb7b80","contentType":"text/yaml"},{"path":"dream_daemon.py","size":3753,"sha256":"aa74743b51a201e9122f70e6e7aebf92f832d4dec08eb729fd8bdab911c503bb","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"fluid_skill.py","size":13130,"sha256":"4ee022e8d6072f7adb91b8e65bd5ee500e4bb8c1373479a0ee0a02fb0225376b","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"hooks/fluid-memory-sync/handler.js","size":1682,"sha256":"ecc976b91142d82f6adccd6b44c3a453b1a46342bc326e0991690546e784b926","contentType":"text/javascript"},{"path":"hooks/fluid-memory-sync/HOOK.md","size":913,"sha256":"7a0ae64fdc42af6adaa11a31f014cebe00646d756a1572a0941095734e481bd1","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"maintenance.py","size":3728,"sha256":"cd3782dd99ac82c03cbac821aaa9042e20c755b96d954072a801b882c82e413e","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"README.md","size":3773,"sha256":"d714a84e4bc292e93fc2127a295156d74a923cf2846ed8a1ac82aea9182217b7","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"SKILL.md","size":2957,"sha256":"13a139f87453a301c26cac6f621541cf246500aad8a0de59edbb6502ecaab8a4","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"wrapper.py","size":2649,"sha256":"db469ed64c019935e5e97d429c9fe6310f92a31fd4219b2c09ec364d03bd91f8","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":2361,"sha256":"df1d08bc0ed9eef088eaf726f25a1bb76cce0b5ceeec31546931e5f6d45ce43c","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"suspicious","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789103491795,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"738bf627a395518e904ff64e16b3f0dccecf91fe7e70582252b1717a060658ca","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/738bf627a395518e904ff64e16b3f0dccecf91fe7e70582252b1717a060658ca","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"clean","verdict":null,"normalizedStatus":"clean","analysis":null,"source":"engines","checkedAt":1780085686012},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":100,"severity":"CRITICAL","recommendation":"DO_NOT_INSTALL","issueCount":33,"checkedAt":1789103491795},"llm":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","confidence":"high","summary":"This local memory skill is not exfiltrating data, but it stores broad chat content in plaintext and has under-disclosed retention and deletion behavior.","dimensions":[{"detail":"Plaintext storage under ~/.openclaw/workspace/database is coherent for a local memory skill, but unbounded raw conversation logging is broader than necessary for summarized memory retention and can expose sensitive chats to local users, tools, or backups.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"Installation is disclosed as a skill plus an optional copied hook, with Python package dependencies chromadb and pyyaml; those dependencies are not pinned to exact versions or hashes.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The skill documents memory triggers and local storage, but the hook behavior is broad, automatic once enabled, and the repeated description of the transcript as temporary is not matched by code that deletes or rotates it.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The skill persists a ChromaDB memory store, summary_buffer.json, and conversation_log.txt; the daemon is long-running if launched, and maintenance performs irreversible deletion inside the skill's memory store without a confirmation or recovery path.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The memory, recall, archive, and decay functions fit the stated fluid-memory purpose, but the hook captures every sent message verbatim into a local transcript and maintenance can permanently delete archived ChromaDB memories after 120 days.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"concern"}],"guidance":"Install only if you are comfortable with a local plaintext memory system. Before enabling the hook, understand that it records sent messages to ~/.openclaw/workspace/database/conversation_log.txt with no built-in retention limit or purge shown in the inspected code. Use disk encryption or strict local permissions, avoid sending secrets while it is enabled, and manually review or delete the database files if you need to clear retained content.","findings":"[T09] unexpected: Accepted in context: the hook appends raw message content to conversation_log.txt and no inspected code clears, rotates, bounds, redacts, or encrypts that file.\n[T08] expected: Accepted as a low-level supply-chain concern: chromadb and pyyaml are expected dependencies for this purpose, but the artifact does not pin versions or hashes.\n[TP4] unexpected: Partially accepted: archiving and decay are purpose-aligned, but maintenance.py also physically deletes archived memories after 120 days, which is not clearly disclosed as permanent deletion.\n[SSD-3] unexpected: Accepted: persistent local memory is expected, but retaining a verbatim transcript of every sent message is broader than the summarized memory function requires.\n[SQP-2] unexpected: Accepted: automatic logging occurs after the hook is enabled, but there is no consent, retention, purge, or sensitive-data handling control in the artifact.\n[SQP-1] expected: Downgraded: recall triggers are normal for a memory assistant and do not by themselves show hidden behavior, though users should understand recall can surface prior stored information.\n[SDI-2] expected: Downgraded: dynamic Python discovery and subprocess execution are ordinary for this wrapper and daemon, with no shell=True or remote payload evidence, but they rely on the local environment.\n[AST4] expected: Downgraded: subprocess calls use argument lists to run bundled local scripts and are consistent with the skill wrapper/maintenance design.\n[SQP-3] expected: Downgraded: Chinese-language UI and documentation are clear from the artifact and are not a security concern by themselves.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789103491795}}}}}